# Every checkout of this repository gets LF, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows installs `core.autocrlf=true` in its SYSTEM config, and the
# GitHub-hosted `windows-latest` image is that same install. Without this file
# a Windows checkout rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF on its way into
# the working tree, while the index stays LF — so the bytes CI compiles are not
# the bytes anyone authored, and a machine whose tree was written by an editor
# rather than checked out (which is every long-lived local clone here) never
# sees it.
#
# On 2026-09-06 that turned main's Windows CI leg red and the Linux leg green,
# with six of `tests/scripts/ciStatus.test.ts`'s eight cases failing on
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`. Vite's SSR transform finds where
# to inject its `__vite_ssr_import__` calls with `hashbangRE = /^#!.*\n/`
# (vite 6.4.3, `dist/node/chunks/dep-Dm0c1Wj2.js`). A JavaScript `.` does not
# match `\r`, so under CRLF that regex misses the shebang, the injection index
# falls back to 0, and the imports are written IN FRONT of `#!/usr/bin/env
# node` — putting a bare `#` in the middle of the module. Eighteen tracked
# scripts start with a shebang; any one of them imported by a test would have
# failed the same way.
#
# `tests/architecture/checkoutLineEndings.test.ts` is the gate. Details in the
# 2026-09-06 entry of docs/learning/defect-register.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-end-convert an asset. `text=auto` already detects these as binary;
# stating it means a detection heuristic cannot corrupt one.
*.png binary
